{"Title":"An Act relative to hot box detectors\r\n","BillNumber":"H3364","DocketNumber":"HD1416","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"KPL1","Name":"Kathleen R. LaNatra","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/KPL1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-11T12:17:40.007"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"KPL1","Name":"Kathleen R. LaNatra","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/KPL1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-11T12:17:40.0066667"},{"Id":"MDB0","Name":"Michael D. Brady","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/MDB0","ResponseDate":"2023-02-01T12:34:24.0333333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H3364/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative LaNatra of Kingston, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 3364) of Kathleen R. LaNatra and Michael D. Brady relative to requiring the installation of hot box detectors every 20 miles on passenger train lines.  Transportation.","DocumentText":"\tSection 176 of said chapter 160 of the General Laws as so appears is hereby amended by inserting after the word \"cars\" the following words:- or tracks and by inserting after the word \"commonwealth\" the following new language:- Hot Box detectors shall be installed every 20 miles on any line in which passenger trains operate. Such shall be included in any new construction project and within one year of the passage of said law on all existing lines.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Favorable","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J27","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J27"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}